# LogRaven — Cursor Project Context

## Project
LogRaven is a cybersecurity SIEM/log analysis platform with two modes:
- Mode 1: Threat Detection (existing) — upload logs, AI finds threats, React dashboard
- Mode 2: SOC 2 Compliance Audit (in progress) — connect AWS, collect evidence, AI maps to SOC 2 controls, generate PDF

## Stack
Backend: FastAPI + Celery + PostgreSQL (SQLAlchemy 2.0) + Redis + Python 3.11
Frontend: React 18 + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS
Dev: Windows + Docker Desktop + WSL2 + PowerShell 7
Deploy: Oracle Cloud (backend) + AWS CloudFront (frontend)
Domain: Namecheap

## AI Integration — MANDATORY RULES
- ALWAYS use: from google import genai
- Client: client = genai.Client()  # reads GEMINI_API_KEY from env
- Async: await client.aio.models.generate_content()
- Model: gemini-2.5-flash
- JSON output: response_mime_type="application/json"
- NEVER use: anthropic, google-generativeai, openai

## Compliance Module Location
app/compliance/
  aws_collector.py    — boto3 STS AssumeRole, CloudTrail, IAM, GuardDuty
  sanitizer.py        — strips PII before AI call
  soc2_mapper.py      — Gemini CC6/CC7 control mapping
  report_generator.py — reportlab PDF builder
  tasks.py            — Celery task pipeline

## UI Colors
Background: #0D1117 | Accent: #2F81F7 | Surface: #161B22
Text: #E6EDF3 | Secondary: #8B949E | Border: #30363D
PASS: #3FB950 | FAIL: #F85149 | PARTIAL: #D29922

## Rules (all modes)
- SQLAlchemy 2.0 select() ONLY — never session.query()
- Pydantic v2 syntax everywhere
- Always async/await in FastAPI routes
- Never load full log file into memory — stream always
- Rule engine FIRST, AI SECOND — AI writes narrative, not detections
- Storage: always use app/utils/storage.py abstraction — never direct file ops
- License validated at main.py startup BEFORE anything else initializes
- pyevtx-rs (pip install evtx) — NOT python-evtx (440x slower)
- mitreattack-python loaded ONCE at module startup — not per request
- Never put business logic in route handlers — use services layer
- JWT access tokens: 15 min expiry. Refresh tokens: 7 days
- UUID primary keys on all new models
- Follow existing patterns in the repo for imports, routers, and tasks
- TypeScript: no any types in new components

## Rules (compliance module only)
- Never use HTML <form> tags — use div + button onClick
- No print() — use the existing logger
- No AWS credentials stored — STS AssumeRole only, time-limited sessions
- No ARNs, IPs, or account IDs sent to Gemini — sanitizer.py handles this
